@startuml panic-safety-boundary
' Fallible-by-construction surface: three partial ops each return Ok/Some (green) or Err/None (red).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  DiamondBackgroundColor #EAECEE
  DiamondBorderColor #707B7C
  DiamondFontColor #2C3E50
  ArrowColor #34495E
  BorderColor #34495E
  BackgroundColor #F2F3F4
}
title Fallible-by-construction public surface — no panics escape

start
:A partial public operation receives caller input;
split
  :weight : f64;
  if (validate_finite_nonnegative_weight:\nfinite and non-negative?) then (ok)
    :Ok(value); <<#2ECC71>>
    stop
  else (NaN / -inf / negative)
    :Err(InvalidWeightError); <<#E74C3C>>
    stop
  endif
split again
  :dict_node, automaton_state, radix M;
  if (try_encode:\nM positive, component below M,\nproduct fits u32?) then (ok)
    :Some(StateId); <<#2ECC71>>
    stop
  else (u32 overflow / out of domain)
    :None  — prune branch; <<#E74C3C>>
    stop
  endif
split again
  :state_id, radix M;
  if (decode:\nradix M nonzero?) then (ok)
    :Some(dict_node, automaton_state); <<#2ECC71>>
    stop
  else (M = 0)
    :None; <<#E74C3C>>
    stop
  endif
end split

legend bottom
  No panics on the public surface: every partial operation returns Result / Option.
  All .expect / .unwrap / panic! sites are confined to #[cfg(test)] modules and doc examples.
end legend
@enduml
